# Minimum statement coverage, in percent. Checked by scripts/coverage.sh; see docs/COVERAGE.md.
#
#   <package-relative-path> <minimum>     a floor from that package's own tests
#   total <minimum>                       the module total, counting cross-package coverage
#   exclude <package> <reason...>         deliberately has no floor
#
# client was LOWERED from 59 to 57 on 2026-10-11, deliberately: the CI runner measures 59.9 for client where development
# machines measure 61.1-62.2 (timing-dependent branches), so a floor of 59 left under a point of margin there.
# codec and total were raised on 2026-10-13 when the SMPP 5.0 fuzz corpus landed (codec 76.2 -> 79.8, total 77.2 -> 78.4),
# and codec again the same day with the error-response encoder fix and its tests (79.8 -> 81.1).
# server and total were raised on 2026-10-11 when the unbound-connection cap and its tests landed (server 75.9 -> 78.3).
# Set 2 points below the values measured on 2026-10-05 (Go 1.22 toolchain, linux/amd64); codec and total
# were raised the same day when the committed fuzz corpus (Task 6.2) lifted codec from 64.8 to 76.0. Measured
# run-to-run noise was under 0.5 points, so the margin is not there for flakiness alone: it also leaves
# room for a small refactor. Raise a floor whenever coverage has risen; lower one only deliberately, in
# a commit that says why.
client     57
codec      79
encoding   72
message    73
protocol   54
server     76
session    80
transport  78
total      76

exclude .                        root package: only architecture/API/posture tests, no statements of its own
exclude cmd/smpp-sim             program, exercised by scripts/acceptance.sh and the examples rather than unit tests
exclude examples/esme            example program
exclude examples/smsc            example program
exclude internal/perflab         benchmark harness
